  '7. A legend is an old traditional story, popularly believed but not proved true. This poem is called a legend because it is an old story told in the Northland to explain why woodpeckers bore wood.',
  '8. (Ten sentences) In the cold Northland, Saint Peter once came to a little old lady’s cottage. He was hungry and tired after fasting. He asked her for a cake. She made a small cake, but it seemed too big to give. She made a smaller one, and then a very thin one, but each seemed too big. She gave him nothing. Saint Peter was angry. He said she was too selfish to live as a human. He turned her into a woodpecker. Now she bores wood all day for her scanty food.',
